            "comment": "No PSSM. BV-BRC holds 69 records under an NS2 string, only 34 of NS2 length, and 24 of those 34 do not end in the right residue -- pestivirus mostly does not cleave NS2-3, and the CSFV reference annotates no NS2 at all. Derived instead from p7's C-terminus to the residue before NS3's N-terminal Gly. That Gly is the Gly1590 of the conserved Arg1589-Gly1590 site (Tautz & Thiel, Arch Virol 2003), present as the motif R|GPAVC in 358 of 400 polyproteins.",
